mission "The Whaler's Log"
    category "side"
    name "The Whaler's Log"
    description "Carry a whaling captain's recovered logbook to his family at Cormorant Quay."
    source "Mermaid's Rest"
    destination "Cormorant Quay"
    reward 460
    speaker offer "Captain Nils Harker"
    speaker visit "Lena Harker"
    speaker complete "Lena Harker"
    on offer
        conversation
            `A broad, quiet whaling captain sets a salt-stained logbook on the table. "My ship is laid up. A split seam and a surgeon's orders. I need this book taken to my sister Lena at Cormorant Quay. It has the last notes my wife made before she died. I would rather it travel in a careful cabin than in a mail sack."`
            choice
                `"I'll see that it reaches her."`
                    accept
                `"I am sorry, but I cannot take it."`
                    close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Whaler's Log. Carry Captain Harker's logbook to Lena Harker at Cormorant Quay."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Lena opens the book and recognises the handwriting at once. She holds it against her chest for a moment before she speaks. "Thank you. He could have sent a hundred letters and none would have meant as much as this."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Lena pays you from the money her brother left for the passage. She refuses to let you leave without a hot meal and a jar of preserved fruit.`
